 # Preview Specifications
 
+## Cache Interface & Deduplication
+
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-001**: When a request identifies an unknown clip revision, the system SHALL return 404 without enqueuing a render job.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-002**: When the requested preview is cached, the system SHALL return 200 with the JPEG for the requested revision and renderer version.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
-- [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+
+## 2Q Eviction — Queue Separation
+
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: The cache SHALL maintain two logical queues: Queue A (new entries) and Queue B (reused entries).
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-011**: Queue A SHALL be capped at 3 GiB (25% of the 12 GiB total capacity). When A reaches this limit and a new entry must be admitted, the oldest entry in A SHALL be evicted by FIFO order.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-012**: Queue B SHALL expand to fill remaining cache capacity up to 9 GiB. Entries in B SHALL be evicted by LRU order when additional space is needed.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-013**: When a cached entry in Queue A receives a second access request, the system SHALL move that entry to Queue B, update its timestamp to the current access time, and remove it from A.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-014**: Subsequent accesses to entries in Queue B SHALL update the entry's LRU timestamp but SHALL NOT move the entry back to Queue A.
+
+## Capacity Management
+
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed the total capacity of 12 GiB, the system SHALL evict entries according to the 2Q policy (FIFO from A if A is at capacity, or LRU from B) before admission to keep the cache within the limit.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-015**: Before admitting a completed JPEG preview to the cache, the system SHALL check whether both Queue A and Queue B are within their respective limits. Eviction proceeds as specified in PREVIEW-011, PREVIEW-012, and PREVIEW-004 until sufficient space exists.
